"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":75.5,"_gate_accruals":-0.07264427883485555,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":70.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.8191521933368995,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.05203143943147698,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":35.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.013342913078170135,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":6.7,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.6661404613364056,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.04371189862044647,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":2.1,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.12610740024853692,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":75.4,"_gate_pool_share":0.16860050945349836,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.005840594567253721,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":27.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.22299974959549185,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.011363770053360246,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":61.4,"_gate_fund_growth":0.06050088776470117,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":60.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06292313001983169,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":81.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.07584026032042923,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02109222474969103,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":64.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.028269999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":18.8,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Covista Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides healthcare education in the United States, Barbados, St. Kitts, and St. Maarten. It operates in three segments: Chamberlain, Walden, and Medical and Veterinary. The company provides degree programs, including bachelor's, master's, and doctoral degrees; and online certificate programs for nursing, health professions, medical, and veterinary postsecondary education, counseling, business, information technology, psychology, public health, social work and human services, public administration and public policy, and criminal justice. It also operates Chamberlain University, Walden University, American University of the Caribbean School of Medicine, Ross University School of Medicine, and Ross University School of Veterinary Medicine. The company was formerly known as Adtalem Global Education Inc. and changed its name to Covista Inc. in February 2026. Covista Inc. was incorporated in 1987 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Stephen W. Beard J.D. | CEO & Chairman | Age 54 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $413K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $83K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Covista Inc. is a mid-cap consumer defensive business with a $3.8B market cap on $2.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $393M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.87\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 8.4\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.8% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 33% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Covista (CVSA) is a Top Growth Stock for the Long-Term","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3035164/why-covista-cvsa-is-a-top-growth-stock-for-the-long-term?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_growth_score-3035164","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795614303.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Covista Inc. (CVSA) Stock Outpacing Its Consumer Discretionary Peers This Year?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3033034/is-covista-inc-cvsa-stock-outpacing-its-consumer-discretionary-peers-this-year?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_1-3033034","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795182003.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Covista (CVSA), Why Is It Drawing Fresh Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nyse-cvsa/covista/news/covista-cvsa-why-is-it-drawing-fresh-attention","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794810163.701,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.691,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's Why Covista (CVSA) is a Strong Value Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029458/here-s-why-covista-cvsa-is-a-strong-value-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_value_score-3029458","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577203.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.691,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"After Plunging 14.7% in 4 Weeks, Here's Why the Trend Might Reverse for Covista (CVSA)","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3026337/after-plunging-14-7-in-4-weeks-here-s-why-the-trend-might-reverse-for-covista-cvsa?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Crsi-3026337","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794231301.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Covista Inc. SVP Douglas G. Beck Sells 362 Shares to Cover RSU Tax Withholding","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemed