.8x depreciation (4.0% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 30, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.8%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 6.3% a year to shareholders (6.3% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 7.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 14.5% of the float, 7.8 days to cover."],"people":["With about 4,736 employees, each generates about $413K of revenue, 0.8x the Consumer Defensive median.","That works out to $83K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.0M (7x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $9K per employee."]},"profile":{"score":51.6,"head":"Trades 33% below fair value of $170; FCF margin 20.1%.","pros":["Composite 52, above the 39 line (gates 14/24)","Trades 33% below fair value of $170","FCF margin 20.1%","Revenue grew 11.9%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.6x"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"vc":{"base":170.34,"base_src":"dcf","bear":61.08,"bull":468.69,"alt_median":76.59,"n_alt":2,"gap":1.224,"dispersion":0.0848,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 122% above the other models' median ($76.59)"]},"med":{"pe":18.0071,"ev_ebitda":10.087,"pfcf":15.0957,"pb":2.0002,"roic":0.1206,"gross_margin":0.3381,"fcf_margin":0.0607,"div_yield":0.0293}},"mc_quantiles":[23.16,45.18,61.08,74.22,89.47,101.48,113.31,129.68,141.94,158.67,175.9,193.72,212.3,239.21,266.84,298.59,341.11,383.24,468.69,623.5,967.7],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.656,"discount_rate":0.025,"terminal_growth":0.003,"exit_multiple":0.002,"base_fcf":0.314},"ticker":"CVSA","date":"2026-11-27"}